{
 "total": 81.547,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "text": "On January fifteenth, nineteen nineteen, a wave tore through Boston.",
   "start": 1.6,
   "end": 5.98
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "It wasn't water.",
   "start": 6.53,
   "end": 7.921
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "It was molasses. Two point three million gallons of it.",
   "start": 8.671,
   "end": 13.398
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "It sat in a steel tank fifty feet tall, on the North End waterfront.",
   "start": 13.898,
   "end": 18.675
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "text": "The tank leaked so badly, the company painted it brown to hide the streaks.",
   "start": 19.125,
   "end": 23.689
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "text": "That morning, the temperature jumped from two degrees to over forty.",
   "start": 24.289,
   "end": 28.333
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "text": "Just after noon, people heard a sound like machine-gun fire. The rivets were popping.",
   "start": 28.933,
   "end": 34.689
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "text": "The tank split open.",
   "start": 35.789,
   "end": 37.395
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "text": "A wall of molasses, twenty-five feet high, rolled through the streets at thirty-five miles an hour.",
   "start": 39.995,
   "end": 46.508
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "text": "It crushed buildings, and knocked a train car off the elevated tracks.",
   "start": 46.908,
   "end": 51.365
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "text": "Then, as the evening air cooled, the molasses thickened, trapping anyone caught inside.",
   "start": 52.265,
   "end": 58.38
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "text": "Twenty-one people died. About a hundred and fifty were injured.",
   "start": 59.58,
   "end": 63.517
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "text": "The harbor stayed brown until summer.",
   "start": 64.417,
   "end": 66.655
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "text": "And the disaster led to rules requiring engineers to sign off on what gets built.",
   "start": 67.355,
   "end": 71.974
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "text": "For decades, locals swore that on hot days, the North End still smelled sweet.",
   "start": 72.774,
   "end": 78.147
  }
 ],
